# Local Codex override example

This optional file is machine-specific and must be copied to
`CODEX_IMPLEMENTATION_PROMPT.local.md`, which is ignored by Git.
It is subordinate to `AGENTS.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`, protected decisions,
accepted ADRs, `BUILD_CHECKLIST.md`, and `CODEX_IMPLEMENTATION_PROMPT.md`.

- Repository path: /absolute/path/to/MethodBridge
- Operating system: macOS or Linux
- Python executable: python3.12
- Virtual environment: .venv
- Container runtime: none or Docker
- Available tools: git, gh, cmake, llama.cpp, adtc-profiler, codex
- Approved local model/cache path: /absolute/local/path
- Target test machine: describe CPU, RAM, OS, and thermal tooling

Local overrides may change paths and commands only. They may not change the
primary user, challenge domain, contribution boundary, held-out split,
human authority, quality gates, or submission-readiness rules.
